## 4. Merge Sorted Array – LeetCode #88

**Difficulty:** Easy

**Concept:** Merge two sorted arrays using three pointers, starting from the end to avoid overwriting elements.

**Time Complexity:** O(m + n)  
**Auxiliary Space Complexity:** O(1)

```java
class Solution {
    public void merge(int[] nums1, int m, int[] nums2, int n) {
        int i = m - 1;
        int j = n - 1;
        int k = m + n - 1;

        while (j >= 0) {
            if (i >= 0 && nums1[i] > nums2[j]) {
                nums1[k] = nums1[i];
                i--;
            } else {
                nums1[k] = nums2[j];
                j--;
            }
            k--;
        }
    }
}
```

[LeetCode Problem](https://leetcode.com/problems/merge-sorted-array/)

